# Line endings, declared once so every clone agrees.
#
# Without this, Git guesses per file from `core.autocrlf`, which is a LOCAL
# setting — and this repo lives in several clones (.master/.win1/.win2), so a
# guess made in one is not the guess made in the next. The symptom is the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" warning on almost
# every commit, and the risk is a whole-file diff when a clone with a different
# setting touches something.
#
# The repo stores LF (it always did) and now checks LF out too, so the working
# tree and the index agree and nothing is rewritten on the way past. Windows
# handles LF fine here: Node, cargo, dotnet, VS Code and PowerShell 7 all read
# it, and the toolchain never shells out to anything that cannot.
* text=auto eol=lf

# …except the ones Windows itself reads. A .ps1/.cmd/.bat with LF is fine for
# PowerShell 7, but keeping these CRLF costs nothing and avoids surprising an
# older host or a double-clicked script. .bat is here for the same reason as
# .cmd — cmd.exe reads both (scripts/watchers/Stream-Helper-DB-to-Creator.bat).
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# POSIX shell keeps LF explicitly: a CRLF `.sh` fails at the shebang under WSL
# and CI, which the blanket rule above already prevents — stated so a future
# per-extension override cannot silently take it away.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Domain payloads. Both are JSON written by `JSON.stringify` (see src/lib/sfcIO.ts
# and src/lib/hsfIO.ts), so they are ordinary text and diff usefully — worth
# saying out loud because the extensions are unknown to Git's own heuristics.
# Some vendor .hsf samples under docs/orig/ carry a UTF-8 BOM; the parser strips
# it on read (hsfIO.ts), so it survives round-trips without a Git rule.
*.sfc text eol=lf
*.hsf text eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.webp  binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.zip   binary
*.db    binary
*.pdn    binary

*.dll   binary
*.zst   binary

# Gear-DB fixtures are generated SQL dumps (scripts/test/gear-db-fixtures.mjs): plain LF
# text so diffs stay readable, collapsed by default in GitHub's diff view.
tests/fixtures/gear-db/*.sql text eol=lf linguist-generated

# SVG is XML, so it stays text and diffs line by line like any other markup.
*.svg text eol=lf

